Truly a heroic effort. I hope your example inspires others to step up and 
keep up the good work.

But in the meanwhile, you've earned your retirement. Thank you!

On Tuesday, June 14, 2016 at 2:07:40 PM UTC-6, Robin Powell wrote:
>
> Yay thank you! 
>
> On Tue, Jun 14, 2016 at 03:27:20PM -0400, Jacob Thomas Errington wrote: 
> > If I were in your area, I'd come buy you a drink. 
> > 
> > Seriously, this is a tremendous project, and you are absolutely 
> deserving of the entire community's respect and acknowledgement. 
> > 
> > Thank you, Robin! 
> > 
> > .i mi'e la tsani mu'o 
> > > On Jun 14, 2016, at 9:41 AM, Robin Lee Powell <
> rlpo...@digitalkingdom.org <javascript:>> wrote: 
> > > 
> > > 
> > > So our EPUB didn't pass any of the automated tests that Ingram Spark 
> > > specified (oops).  This led to major revisions in terms of the 
> > > markup details of all versions except the PDF, but especially the 
> > > EPUB.  We now roll our own EPUB by hand (it turns out it's just a 
> > > specially formatted zip file with XHTML in it, so we just use the 
> > > section-chunked version of the CLL plus a bunch of post-processing). 
> > > 
> > > There were also some bug fixes to the content; see 
> > > http://lojban.org/publications/cll/CHANGELOG for complete details of 
> > > the latest revision.  Props to 101001000100001 for the great catch 
> > > (we had things like "Example 5.5" in a few places that were raw text 
> > > instead of links, and hence completely wrong). 
> > > 
> > > Oh, also, I added a changelog.  :D 
> > > 
> > > I have just uploaded the EPUB and print versions 2016-06-12 to 
> > > Ingram Spark. 
> > > 
> > > Assuming that all goes well with those uploads (and in particular 
> > > that they show up on Amazon as two versions of the same book, a 
> > > point abuot which I am extremely skeptical), I'm pretty much done 
> > > with CLL work. 
> > > 
> > > Like, "hey Robin you're the one most familiar with the process can 
> > > you roll new versions?" is fine, but I've lost literally hundreds 
> > > (probably over a thousand) hours of my life to this thing, so now 
> > > that it's up and running I'm basically out. 
